  "describe": "On Thursday 29 October 2026 the labels read \"Thursday, 29 October 2026\", \"Thu 29 Oct\" (centred), \"29 Oct 2026\", \"2026-10-29\" (blue), \"29/10/2026\" and \"10/29/2026\" (end-aligned). On Sunday 3 January 2027 (the january render) the names change to \"Sunday, 3 January 2027\" and \"Sun 3 Jan\". Each label fills the column's width: at 200 dp the 18 dp long date is wider than the column and is scaled down to fit on its line; at 420 dp the centred and end-aligned ones follow the width. A screen reader announces each date in words with full names: \"Thursday, 29 October 2026\", \"Thursday 29 October\", \"29 October 2026\" (medium, iso, dmy) and \"October 29, 2026\" (mdy).",
